{"author":{"id":"3e9eecde2ef772d1feab6941c5c5e71771dbb72558288071e814db7ee77e87b5"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789063156,"nonce":"ACJjYMLtWL+rwwm9hLBQQDQRrqE=","title":"Session metadata: free-form key/values with well-known keys (jira, description)","message":"Associate arbitrary metadata with a session, e.g. a description or a Jira ticket, so UIs can surface and act on it (extract a Jira key, open the ticket).\n\nDecisions (clarified 2026-09-10):\n\n- Entry point: editable via CLI after launch — shep meta \u003cagent\u003e key=value (no launch flags, no auto-detection, no hook-reported metadata for v1).\n- Schema: free-form key/values pass through untouched; well-known keys get typed treatment in UIs: jira (clickable link, base URL configurable), description (prominent display), url.\n- Persistence: keyed by the agent's resumable session id (agent_session) — metadata follows the session across shep runs and server restarts. Note: this is shepherd's first durable state; today the server is memory-only. Needs a small on-disk store re-keyed on session registration.\n- Surfaces (v1): web monitor card, Raycast extension (subtitle + open-ticket action), shep status table. SwiftBar out of scope.\n\nRelationship to existing model: AgentInfo already has state_labels (free-form key/values from integrations). Decide whether user metadata merges into state_labels or is a sibling field (e.g. metadata) — sibling is likely cleaner since provenance and persistence differ.","files":null}]}